## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to reason about cost-benefit tradeoffs for on-device prefetching and privacy-friendly design in a beginner-friendly context.

## Key Concepts
- On-device caching and prefetching strategies
- Resource budgets: energy, memory, data
- Privacy and consent controls
- Observability: cache hit rate, latency, drift
- Rollout strategy and break-even planning

## Code Example
```javascript
// Lightweight prefetch example (pseudo)
async function prefetchAssets(urls, cache) {
  for (const u of urls) {
    try {
      const resp = await fetch(u, {mode: 'no-cors', credentials: 'omit'});
      if (resp.ok) await cache.put(u, resp.clone());
    } catch (e) { /* ignore */ }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you measure energy impact on mobile vs desktop?
- How would you ensure privacy compliance and opt-in UX for prefetching?

## Why This Is Asked
New angle on CBA: gating cross‑app features via an on‑device policy engine, balancing UX, energy, and safety with cloud updates.

## Key Concepts
- On‑device policy engines and gating rules
- Resource awareness (battery, thermal, memory)
- Telemetry footprint and privacy compliance
- Rollout strategy and break‑even analysis

## Code Example
```javascript
function shouldRunFeature(state, policy) {
  if (state.battery < 20) return false;
  if (state.temperature > 45) return false;
  if (state.freeMemory < 200) return false;
  return policy.allowsFeature;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you quantify risk of safety incidents vs false positives?
- What metrics would drive policy update cadence and rollouts across device generations?

